@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Creating a Database";
}

<section>

    <!-- =====================================================
         PAGE INTRODUCTION
         ===================================================== -->

    <div class="mb-5">

        <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Creating a Database
        </h1>

        <p class="lead text-muted">
            In SQL Server, the CREATE DATABASE statement is used to
            create a new database. A database provides a container
            where tables and other database objects can be stored.
        </p>

    </div>


    <!-- =====================================================
         WHAT IS CREATE DATABASE?
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            What is CREATE DATABASE?
        </h2>

        <p>
            The <strong>CREATE DATABASE</strong> statement creates a
            new database in SQL Server.
        </p>

        <p>
            Once a database is created, we can create tables and other
            database objects inside it.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE DATABASE CollegeDB;</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         DATABASE CREATION FLOW
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Database Creation Flow
        </h2>

        <p>
            The basic process of creating a database can be understood
            as follows:
        </p>

        <div class="code-block">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL Server
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>
                                                             SQL Server
                                                                 ↓
                                                             CREATE DATABASE
                                                                 ↓
                                                             CollegeDB
                                                                 ↓
                                                            Create Tables
                                                                 ↓
                                                             Insert Data</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         SIMPLE DATABASE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Create a Simple Database
        </h2>

        <p>
            The following statement creates a database named
            <strong>StudentDB</strong>.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE DATABASE StudentDB;</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p>
            After executing the statement, SQL Server creates the
            <strong>StudentDB</strong> database.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         VERIFY DATABASE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Verify the Database
        </h2>

        <p>
            We can check whether the database exists by using the
            following query:
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>SELECT name
FROM sys.databases;</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p>
            This query displays the databases available on the SQL
            Server instance.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         OUTPUT
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Output
        </h2>

        <p>
            After executing the query, the database name can be seen
            in the result.
        </p>

        <div class="table-responsive">

            <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">

                <thead class="table-dark">

                    <tr>
                        <th>Database Name</th>
                    </tr>

                </thead>

                <tbody>

                    <tr>
                        <td>master</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>model</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>msdb</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>tempdb</td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>StudentDB</strong></td>
                    </tr>

                </tbody>

            </table>

        </div>

        <p class="text-muted mt-3">
            The exact list of databases depends on the SQL Server
            installation and databases available on the server.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         USE DATABASE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Select a Database Using USE
        </h2>

        <p>
            After creating a database, the <strong>USE</strong>
            statement can be used to select that database for
            subsequent SQL operations.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>USE StudentDB;</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p>
            After executing this statement, subsequent table creation
            statements will be executed in the selected database.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         CREATE DATABASE + TABLE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Create Database and Table
        </h2>

        <p>
            We can create a database first and then create a table
            inside that database.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>CREATE DATABASE StudentDB;

USE StudentDB;

CREATE TABLE Students
(
    StudentId INT,
    StudentName VARCHAR(100),
    Age INT,
    Course VARCHAR(50)
);</code></pre>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         DATABASE OBJECTS
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            What Can a Database Contain?
        </h2>

        <p>
            A SQL Server database can contain different types of
            database objects.
        </p>

        <div class="row g-3">

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        Tables
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Store data in rows and columns.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        Views
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Provide a way to query data through a saved
                        query definition.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        Stored Procedures
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Store reusable SQL statements and logic.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        Functions
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Perform reusable operations and return values.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        Indexes
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Help SQL Server locate data efficiently.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">

                <div class="border rounded-3 p-4 h-100 bg-light">

                    <h5 class="fw-bold">
                        Constraints
                    </h5>

                    <p class="mb-0 text-muted">
                        Help enforce rules on table data.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         IF NOT EXISTS
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Check Before Creating a Database
        </h2>

        <p>
            Before creating a database, we can check whether a database
            with the same name already exists.
        </p>

        <div class="code-block mb-3">

            <div class="code-lang-tag">
                SQL
            </div>

            <pre class="mb-0"><code>IF DB_ID('TrainingDB') IS NULL
BEGIN
    CREATE DATABASE TrainingDB;
END;</code></pre>

        </div>

        <p>
            This prevents the CREATE DATABASE statement from being
            executed when the specified database already exists.
        </p>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         DATABASE NAMING
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            Database Naming Guidelines
        </h2>

        <ul>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Choose a meaningful database name.
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Keep naming consistent across the project.
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Avoid unnecessarily complicated names.
            </li>

            <li class="mb-2">
                Use names that clearly describe the application's data.
            </li>

        </ul>

        <div class="alert alert-info border-0">

            <strong>Example:</strong>

            <span>
                StudentManagementDB
            </span>

            is more descriptive than a name such as
            <strong>DB1</strong>.

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         IMPORTANT NOTE
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-5">

        <div class="alert alert-warning border-0">

            <h5 class="fw-bold">
                Important
            </h5>

            <p class="mb-0">
                A database should be created with a meaningful name
                and should be organized properly before creating the
                application's tables and other database objects.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


    <!-- =====================================================
         SUMMARY
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="mb-4">

        <div class="alert alert-primary border-0">

            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                Summary
            </h2>

            <p class="mb-0">
                In this section, we learned how to create a database
                using CREATE DATABASE, verify databases using
                sys.databases, select a database using USE and create
                tables inside the selected database.
            </p>

        </div>

    </section>


